# KNOWN GAP — an INLINE STRUCT CONSTRUCTOR inside an f-string interpolation
# lowers as a TUPLE. `gg check` is clean; C refuses to compile; LLVM compiles
# and prints GARBAGE.
#
#     print(f"{A(7).x}")     # <- the defect
#     print(A(7).x)          # <- the CONTROL: correct, prints 7
#
#     gg check : rc 0, clean
#     C  build : rc 1, `error: '__gg_A' has no member named '_0'`
#     LLVM     : build rc 0, run rc 0, prints 187650551193044  (GARBAGE)
#
# The `_0` in the C error is the tell: `_0` is TUPLE field naming, so the
# inline `A(7)` was lowered as an anonymous product instead of the named
# struct. No `==` and no equality machinery is involved.
#
# DISCRIMINATOR: the f-string wrapper ALONE. The identical expression outside
# an f-string is correct on both lanes. Do not vary anything else when
# reproducing.
#
# ⇒ Core #8: broken on BOTH lanes in two DIFFERENT ways -- a build refusal on
# C and a silent wrong VALUE on LLVM. That is >=2 bugs and a lane divergence,
# not one backend's problem. The LLVM half is the worse one: rc 0, no
# diagnostic, plausible-looking garbage.
#
# DISTINCT FROM `t0162`, its sibling in the same family -- state the
# discriminator before merging them:
#   * `t0162` is a SELF-HOST lane gap about an ITERATOR TERMINAL called inline
#     inside an f-string interpolation.
#   * THIS is the RUST lane, and the inline expression is a STRUCT
#     CONSTRUCTOR mis-lowered as a tuple. Different lane, different construct.
#
# ⚠ METHODOLOGICAL CONSEQUENCE, and the reason this was found: this tree's
# standing probe-hygiene rule says NEVER test accept/reject inside an f-string,
# because a rejected expression reads as ACCEPTED. This gap is the same hazard
# in its POSITIVE form -- the f-string does not merely mask a diagnostic, it
# CHANGES THE LOWERING. Any fixture that observes a value through an f-string
# is measuring a different program than the one it appears to test.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints 7, on BOTH backends.
# Measured 2026-08-27 at HEAD by the R45 Track B scout; orchestrator-verified
# on both lanes, with the non-f-string control run alongside.

struct A:
    int x

void main():
    print(f"{A(7).x}")
